>From 25447598a2ab0e6ab71c57621a2c9c9cae4c3140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Niedermayer <michael@niedermayer.cc>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:41:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tests/swscale: compare unscaled conversion across thread
 counts
Compare one-thread conversion with 2, 3, 7 and 16 threads for five even
frame heights, including cases that otherwise produce odd slices. Cover
NV12, NV21, YUV420P, YUVA420P and YUV422P to packed and planar RGB,
including both byte orders of the 16-bit formats.
Exercise both dynamic and initialized legacy swscale contexts. Disable
dithering so the AArch64 selector must supply its own slice alignment
for planar inputs as well. Compare within each implementation to avoid
requiring identical color conversion rounding across architectures.
Print mismatching row counts for FATE to compare with its reference.
The test fails before the preceding fix on native AArch64 and passes
afterwards. It also passes on native x86-64.
Assisted-by: Fairy
---
 libswscale/Makefile                  |   1 +
 libswscale/tests/.gitignore          |   1 +
 libswscale/tests/unscaled_threaded.c | 148 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
